# User groups (bootloader — spec in `docs/modules/user-groups.md`, ADR-020)

Groups are another input to `authz.compute_levels`, not a copy of SMS or of `user_subject_permissions`.

## Invariants

- Effective level on a subject = highest of personal grant, every group the user belongs to (`authz.highest_grant`), and SMS (existing issuer cap). A group never lowers another source.
- A group role is only `viewer` / `user` / `admin`. It cannot grant super admin (`users.is_super_admin`).
- Never write SMS rows into `user_group_permissions` or `user_subject_permissions`. Never write a group grant back onto those tables.
- Both `authz._load_levels` and `users_directory._ranks` pass `groups`. The SMS-only column passes an empty map. A new level source goes into `compute_levels`, then both of those loaders.
- Do not bump `session_version` on a group edit. Levels are not in the session.
- Subject delete removes `user_group_permissions` for that subject (no FK cascade). User erase removes that user's `user_group_members` row (`user_erase.LINKS`); the group stays.
- Routes: `@login_required` + `@super_admin_required`. Service raises `GroupError`; the route translates `code` and commits.

## Gotchas

- `highest_grant` drops unknown roles. Do not store them.
- A disabled account still has no effective level. Membership stays.
